{"kind":"stack","id":"s-circuits","title":"Will the lamp light? Simple circuits","theme":{"background":"#fdf6e3","foreground":"#1f2933","font":"Arial, sans-serif"}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c1","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c1-t","content":"Complete circuit"},{"type":"text","id":"c1-d","content":"A closed loop that goes from one end of the battery, through the lamp and back to the other end of the battery. Electricity can flow all the way round."},{"type":"button","id":"c1-b","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c2"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c2","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c2-t","content":"Open circuit"},{"type":"text","id":"c2-d","content":"A circuit with a gap in it, so the loop is broken. Electricity cannot flow round, and the lamp stays off."},{"type":"button","id":"c2-b","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c3"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c3","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c3-q","content":"A battery and a lamp are connected by two wires in a closed loop. Does the lamp light?"},{"type":"button","id":"c3-a","label":"No, the lamp stays off","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-b","label":"Yes, the lamp lights","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-c","label":"Only if the wires are thick","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c4","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c4-q","content":"One wire has been cut in half. The loop is broken. Does the lamp light?"},{"type":"button","id":"c4-a","label":"Yes, it lights up brightly","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c4-b","label":"No, the lamp stays off","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c4-c","label":"It flickers but does not fully light","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c4-d","label":"It lights for one second, then goes off","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c5","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c5-q","content":"A lamp is connected to only one end of the battery, with no wire to the other end. Does it light?"},{"type":"button","id":"c5-a","label":"Yes, one wire is enough","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c5-b","label":"No, there is no complete loop","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c5-c","label":"Yes, if the battery is new","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c6","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c6-q","content":"Your torch is broken. The lamp will not light. Which path will you take to find the fault?"},{"type":"button","id":"c6-a","label":"Check the switch is on, then check the wires","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c7"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c6-b","label":"Shake the torch hard and hope for the best","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c8"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c7","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c7-t","content":"You find the switch was off. You switch it on, and the lamp lights. You check the loop is whole, and you learn the lesson: check for a complete loop first."},{"type":"button","id":"c7-b","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c8","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c8-t","content":"Shaking does nothing. The loop is still broken. You stop and think, then trace the wires and find a gap. You learn to check the loop, not just shake the torch."},{"type":"button","id":"c8-b","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c9","kind":"end","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c9-h","content":"You finished the circuits lesson"},{"type":"text","id":"c9-m","content":"Well done. Remember: the lamp lights only when the battery, lamp and wires form one complete loop."}],"actions":[]}}
